@startuml sequence
title Auth0 login to Google Cloud Storage with Workload Identity Federation

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9B458

actor User
participant "SPA\n(browser)" as SPA
participant "Auth0\n(custom domain)" as Auth0
participant "Google STS\nsts.googleapis.com" as STS
participant "Cloud Storage" as GCS

== 1. Log in with Auth0 ==
User -> SPA : Open the app
User -> SPA : Click "Log in with Auth0"
SPA -> Auth0 : GET /authorize\n(client_id = SPA, audience = API, PKCE challenge)
Auth0 -> User : Login page
User -> Auth0 : Credentials
Auth0 --> SPA : Redirect back with ?code=...
SPA -> Auth0 : POST /oauth/token (code + PKCE verifier)
Auth0 --> SPA : Access token (JWT)
note right of Auth0
  iss = https://<custom domain>/
  aud = [API audience, /userinfo]
  azp = SPA client ID
  sub = auth0|<user id>
end note

== 2. Exchange the token for a Google access token ==
SPA -> STS : POST /v1/token (RFC 8693 token exchange)\naudience = workload identity provider, subject_token = access token\n**unauthenticated: no Google credentials in the browser**
STS -> Auth0 : Fetch OIDC discovery + JWKS\n(from the provider's issuer_uri)
Auth0 --> STS : Signing keys
note over STS
  Workload identity provider checks:
  1. signature and iss match the provider's issuer_uri
  2. aud contains an allowed_audiences entry (our API)
     (rejects ID tokens and tokens for other APIs)
  3. attribute_condition: azp is the SPA or CLI client ID
  Then google.subject = sub.
end note
STS --> SPA : Federated access token (about 1 hour)

== 3. Use Cloud Storage with the federated token ==
SPA -> GCS : GET /storage/v1/b/<bucket>/o?prefix=users/<sub>/\nAuthorization: Bearer <federated token>
GCS --> SPA : Your objects
User -> SPA : Choose a file and upload
SPA -> GCS : POST /upload/storage/v1/b/<bucket>/o?name=users/<sub>/<file>
GCS --> SPA : 200 OK
note over GCS
  The pool principal itself holds roles/storage.objectUser on the bucket
  (direct access, no service account impersonation).
  Unlike the AWS demo this grant is pool-wide: no per-user prefix isolation.
end note

== 4. Token expires ==
SPA -> Auth0 : getTokenSilently() when the federated token is within 5 minutes of expiry
Auth0 --> SPA : New access token
SPA -> STS : Token exchange (as in step 2)

@enduml
